{"name":"Crop Circle","hex":"#e9bf63","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crop circle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An area in a field of crops where the stalks have been flattened into a circle or other geometric shape, performed as a prank or sometimes ascribed to UFO activity etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crop_circle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crop circle","blocks":[{"text":"A crop circle, crop formation, or corn circle is a pattern created by flattening a crop, usually a cereal. The term was coined in the early 1980s. Crop circles have been described as all falling \"within the range of the sort of thing done in hoaxes\" by Taner Edis, professor of physics at Truman State University."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/CropCircleW.jpg/330px-CropCircleW.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crop_circle"},{"title":"Crop Circle (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Crop Circle is the second studio album by English rapper Nines. It was released on 20 April 2018 by XL Recordings. It is the follow-up to Nines' debut album One Foot Out (2017), which peaked at number 4 on the UK Albums Chart. The album features guest appearances from Dave, Ray BLK, Haile, Tiggs da Author and numerous Ice City Boyz members. Production is handled by 5ive Beatz, Steel Banglez, Beatfreakz, Pinero Beats, Show N Prove and Zeph Ellis."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d8/Crop_Circle_by_Nines.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crop_Circle_(album)"},{"title":"Crop","blocks":[{"text":"A crop is a plant or plant product harvested for human use. Crops are cultivated at scale to produce food, fiber, fuel, and other products. Crops have been central to human civilization since the first agricultural revolution, a key stage in the broader history of agriculture, when early societies domesticated plants for food and trade. Today, a small number of staple crops such as rice, wheat, maize, and sugarcane account for the majority of global production. Because of their economic importance, crops are studied within several scientific disciplines, including agronomy, agricultural science, horticulture, and forestry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Orange-tree-1117423.jpg/330px-Orange-tree-1117423.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crop"},{"title":"Circle","blocks":[{"text":"A circle is a shape consisting of all points in a plane that are at a given distance from a given point, the centre. The distance between any point of the circle and the centre is called the radius. The length of a line segment connecting two points on the circle and passing through the centre is called the diameter. A circle bounds a region of the plane called a disc."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Circle-withsegments.svg/330px-Circle-withsegments.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circle"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Aerial_View_of_the_Crop_Circle_in_Diessenhofen_15.07.2008_16-44-41.JPG/500px-Aerial_View_of_the_Crop_Circle_in_Diessenhofen_15.07.2008_16-44-41.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Aerial_View_of_the_Crop_Circle_in_Diessenhofen_15.07.2008_16-44-41.JPG/500px-Aerial_View_of_the_Crop_Circle_in_Diessenhofen_15.07.2008_16-44-41.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aerial view of a crop circle in Diessenhofen","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAerial_View_of_the_Crop_Circle_in_Diessenhofen_15.07.2008_16-44-41.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Swiss_crop_circle_detail.jpg/500px-Swiss_crop_circle_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Swiss_crop_circle_detail.jpg/1280px-Swiss_crop_circle_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Swiss_crop_circle_detail.jpg/500px-Swiss_crop_circle_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Detail of a crop circle in a field in Switzerland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASwiss_crop_circle_detail.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Colour_sketch_of_a_spaceship_creating_crop_circles.jpg/500px-Colour_sketch_of_a_spaceship_creating_crop_circles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Colour_sketch_of_a_spaceship_creating_crop_circles.jpg/500px-Colour_sketch_of_a_spaceship_creating_crop_circles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sketch of a \"spaceship\" creating crop circles, sent to UK Ministry of Defence circa 1998","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AColour_sketch_of_a_spaceship_creating_crop_circles.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Diablefaucheur.jpg/330px-Diablefaucheur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Diablefaucheur.jpg/330px-Diablefaucheur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1678 pamphlet on the \"Mowing-Devil\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADiablefaucheur.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/